.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
\fBAnimated\fP view owned by a \fBPort\fP or shared by layers\&. 

Scene-owned cameras advance on their scene clock\&. Layer overrides remain available; \fBScene\fP describes ownership and pause behavior\&.

.PP
See \fBCamera visibility, fades and transitions\fP for camera visibility, composed opacity, fades and crossfades\&.

.PP
\fBCamera\fP inherits \fBEventEmitter\fP event handling and \fBAnimated\fP movement, rotation, scale, reflection, pivots, helpers, timed chains and schedule controls\&. Moving its location right moves visible world content left\&. Rotation uses radians and is inverted in the view; zoom and scale magnify content\&. \fBCamera\fP size is animation metadata and does not resize a viewport\&. For a Port-owned camera, location + centerOffset maps to the \fBPort\fP anchor, in port coordinates\&. Anchors default to (0,0)\&. An explicit layer camera maps its focus to the center of its stored viewport\&.

.PP
A layer's explicit camera overrides its \fBScene\fP camera and port camera\&. Clearing the explicit camera restores inheritance from its \fBScene\fP, or from the current \fBPort\fP for a legacy layer\&. Every \fBPort\fP owns its camera\&. Attachments retain cameras; getCamera()/getEffectiveCamera() preserve shared JavaScript identity\&. Attached cameras advance once per runtime tick regardless of attachment count or whether a layer is paused or hidden\&. Scene-owned cameras advance on scene time and stop when their scene pauses\&. animate(seconds) additionally advances state, and is intended for manual/detached animation\&.

.PP
Direct \fBPort\fP Renderer drawing applies the camera once outside local \fBAttributes\fP transforms, including nested Drawings\&. Layers project sprites, Parts, particles and tiles through their effective camera once\&. \fBPort\fP clipping and clear operations remain in port coordinates\&. MVC Views automatically draw in screen space\&. For direct screen drawing, disable camera drawing temporarily and restore it in finally\&. \fBPort\fP conversions still use the camera while drawing is disabled\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBPort\fP attachment and rendering require a graphics-capable build\&. \fBCamera\fP animation and explicit layer attachments also work headlessly\&. \fBCamera\fP zoom must stay finite and positive, and its view must have finite, nonzero scale\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const camera = port\&.getCamera();
port\&.setCameraAnchor(new pdg\&.Point(320, 240));
const actors = pdg\&.createSpriteLayer(port);
const background = pdg\&.createSpriteLayer(port);
background\&.setCameraParallax(0\&.5, 0);
camera\&.setLocation(100, 200)\&.zoomTo(2, 0\&.5, pdg\&.linearTween);
// Both layers inherit camera; background ignores zoom and scrolls half as far\&.
.fi
.PP
 
