.SS "\fBCamera\fP cutTo (\fBCamera\fP destination)"

.PP
Schedule an atomic camera visibility and picking handoff\&. Hide this camera and show the destination at the scheduled instant, without a blended frame\&. Position, zoom, opacity, animation and following remain unchanged\&. The cut is immediate unless delayed by \fBwait()\fP or placed after an operation using \fBandThen()\fP\&. A paused schedule delays execution; cancellation before execution leaves both cameras' visibility unchanged\&. Cancelling after execution does not undo the cut\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdestination\fP A distinct output \fBCamera\fP\&. It may use another viewport or \fBPort\fP, or be unattached; cuts also work in headless builds\&. Effects-stage cameras cannot participate\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This camera for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
A pending cut retains the destination and reserves both cameras against other handoffs\&. Pending cuts cannot be serialized, repeated, reversed or replayed with \fBrestartIt()\fP; request a new cut after completion or cancellation\&. Removing either camera's last attachment cancels a pending cut\&. Unlike blended transitions, cuts do not require contiguous scene pairs or matching viewports\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
source\&.wait(0\&.5)\&.cutTo(destination);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
