.SS "\fBCamera\fP lumaFadeTo (\fBCamera\fP destination, number seconds, \fBImage\fP mask = \fRnull\fP, number softness = \fR0\&.1\fP, boolean darkFirst = \fRfalse\fP, int easing = \fR\fBeaseInOutQuad\fP\fP)"

.PP
Reveal a live destination using a frozen luminance mask\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fReasing:\fP \fBEasingFunction\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
The mask stretches to the common viewport using nearest sampling\&. Luminance is computed from straight RGB in linear color space; fully transparent pixels have zero luminance\&. The mask is frozen at the first rendered transition frame, while both scene images remain live\&. Without an explicit mask, that first source-camera image supplies it\&. Supplied images are retained until completion or cancellation\&. On resize, the frozen mask stretches to the new viewport\&. Progress endpoints show the complete source and destination even for uniform black or white masks\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdestination\fP Distinct camera attached to the same \fBPort\fP with the same nonempty viewport\&. 
.br
\fIseconds\fP Finite nonnegative duration in seconds\&. 
.br
\fImask\fP Optional \fBImage\fP, or null to derive the mask from the initial source output\&. 
.br
\fIsoftness\fP Reveal-band width in linear luminance units, from 0 to 1; defaults to 0\&.1\&. Zero gives a hard edge\&. 
.br
\fIdarkFirst\fP False reveals bright pixels first; true reveals dark pixels first\&. 
.br
\fIeasing\fP Easing function; defaults to easeInOutQuad\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This camera for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBScene\fP layers must remain contiguous\&. The source receives picking throughout the transition; completion hides it and shows the destination\&. Shared transition pause, queue, cancellation and snapshot restrictions apply\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
source\&.lumaFadeTo(destination, 1\&.0, null, 0\&.15, false, pdg\&.linearTween);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBtransitionTo()\fP, \fBwhipPanTo()\fP, \fBCamera visibility, fades and transitions\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
