.SS "\fBCamera\fP matchCutTo (\fBCamera\fP destination, \fBCameraMatchCutOptions\fP options)"

.PP
Match two \fBSprite\fP compositions and preserve apparent motion across a hard cut\&. The mode names the reference shot and whether to match size\&. During the approach, \fRmode: \fBpdg\&.matchSource\fP\fP preserves the outgoing shot and aligns the hidden incoming camera so matchTarget reaches matchSource's live \fBPort\fP position\&. \fRmode: \fBpdg\&.matchTarget\fP\fP eases the outgoing camera so matchSource reaches matchTarget's live \fBPort\fP position\&. At the cut the engine matches projected bounds centers, apparent velocity and, with an AndSize mode, apparent size and its rate of change\&. Size means the largest dimension of the projected \fBSprite\fP bounds; rotation and aspect ratio are preserved\&.

.PP
The source schedule owns the approach and settling phases\&. Both cameras remain reserved until settling finishes; \fBandThen()\fP starts its successor afterward\&. Visibility and picking switch at the approach boundary\&. \fBwait()\fP, \fBpauseSchedule()\fP, \fBresumeSchedule()\fP, \fBcancelSchedule()\fP and \fBstopIt()\fP apply to the whole operation\&. Cancellation before the cut removes matching adjustments and restores visibility\&. Cancellation after the cut retains the incoming view at its current framing\&. Removed/reassigned subjects or detached cameras cancel safely\&. Pending operations retain the destination, check \fBSprite\fP lifetimes and cannot be saved as snapshots, repeated, reversed or restarted\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdestination\fP Incoming camera, retained until completion or cancellation\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP Matching settings described below\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This source camera for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
 
.PP
\fBMatching options\fP
.RS 4

.RE
.PP
Field  Default  Meaning  matchSource  Required  \fBSprite\fP belonging to the source camera\&.  matchTarget  Required  Distinct \fBSprite\fP belonging to the destination camera\&.  mode  matchSource  \fBCamera\fP matching enum; see the four modes below\&.  approachSeconds  0\&.4  Finite positive time to synchronize the scenes before the cut or fade\&.  settleSeconds  0\&.4  Finite positive time to ease out inherited camera motion after the cut or fade\&.  settleReturnsCamera  false  Retain the matched framing and deceleration travel\&. Set true to restore the incoming base framing/zoom or its live following view\&.  approachEasing  easeInQuad  Registered monotonic easing with zero/one endpoints\&.  settleEasing  easeOutQuad  Registered monotonic easing controlling the decay of extra motion\&.  

.PP
Mode  Behavior  \fBpdg\&.matchSource\fP  Preserve the source shot; align the incoming camera's position and apparent motion without adjusting zoom\&.  \fBpdg\&.matchSourceAndSize\fP  Match the source shot, also matching apparent size and its rate using zoom\&.  \fBpdg\&.matchTarget\fP  Move the outgoing camera toward the target shot without adjusting zoom\&.  \fBpdg\&.matchTargetAndSize\fP  Approach the target shot's position and size; carry apparent motion and size rate through the cut\&.  

.PP

.PP
Following and independent camera effects continue\&. Keeping matched framing also retains the resulting following offset\&. Matching corrections compose with the camera's live base position and zoom; settleReturnsCamera removes those corrections at completion\&. The matchSource and matchTarget modes leave zoom unchanged\&. \fBgetLocation()\fP and \fBgetZoom()\fP expose the base pose while temporary matching corrections are active; layer coordinate conversions include those corrections\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires graphics, Sprites on layers sharing a \fBPort\fP and identical nonempty camera viewports\&. Translation parallax must be nonzero; zoom matching also needs nonzero zoom parallax and nonempty projected bounds\&. Pixel snapping and view-bounds clamping are unsupported for either matched camera\&. Use logical \fBSprite\fP bounds that describe the artwork being matched\&. Overshooting or reversing easings throw\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
// Source and target Sprites belong to the respective cameras on the same Port\&.
sourceCamera\&.matchCutTo(destinationCamera, {
    matchSource: sourceSprite,
    matchTarget: targetSprite,
    mode: pdg\&.matchSourceAndSize,
    settleReturnsCamera: true,
    approachSeconds: 0\&.4,
    settleSeconds: 0\&.6
});

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBcutTo()\fP, \fBCamera visibility, fades and transitions\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
