.SS "\fBCamera\fP matchFadeTo (\fBCamera\fP destination, \fBCameraMatchFadeOptions\fP options)"

.PP
Synchronize two \fBSprite\fP compositions, crossfade while matched, then settle\&. Uses the modes and matching settings in \fBcamera_match_options\fP\&. After the approach synchronizes the scenes, both live scenes crossfade\&. Their \fBSprite\fP bounds centers remain aligned throughout the blend; AndSize modes also maintain equal projected bounds size\&. The outgoing camera carries its approach motion through the fade\&. At the fade endpoint the destination inherits apparent motion and settles with the same behavior as \fBmatchCutTo()\fP\&. Following, \fBSprite\fP motion and camera effects continue during all three phases\&.

.PP
The source schedule owns approach, fade and settling\&. Both cameras remain reserved until settling finishes; \fBandThen()\fP follows all three phases\&. Picking uses the source during the fade and switches to the destination when fading ends\&. Pausing freezes the operation\&. Cancellation during approach or fade restores original visibility and removes matching corrections; cancellation during settling retains the incoming framing\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdestination\fP Incoming camera, retained until completion or cancellation\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP All settings in \fBcamera_match_options\fP, plus the fade settings below\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This source camera for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
 
.PP
\fBAdditional matched-fade options\fP
.RS 4

.RE
.PP
Field  Default  Meaning  fadeSeconds  0\&.4  Finite positive blend duration in seconds, between approach and settling\&.  fadeEasing  linearTween  Registered monotonic easing with zero/one endpoints controlling the blend\&.  

.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires the same \fBSprite\fP, \fBPort\fP, viewport and parallax setup as \fBmatchCutTo()\fP\&. Each camera's layers must form a contiguous scene on their shared \fBPort\fP, as for \fBtransitionTo()\fP\&. Interleaved scenes and unrelated layers between the scenes throw\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
// These Sprites belong to the two cameras on the same Port\&.
sourceCamera\&.matchFadeTo(destinationCamera, {
    matchSource: sourceSprite,
    matchTarget: targetSprite,
    mode: pdg\&.matchSourceAndSize,
    approachSeconds: 0\&.4,
    fadeSeconds: 0\&.6,
    settleSeconds: 0\&.4
});

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBmatchCutTo()\fP, \fBtransitionTo()\fP, \fBcamera_match_options\fP 
.RE
.PP

