.SS "\fBIEventHandler\fP onZoomComplete (function callback)"

.PP
Listen for this camera's completed zoom operations\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fRcallback:\fP \fBCameraZoomEventCallback\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcallback\fP Function called synchronously with a CameraZoomInfo event\&. Its fields are camera, zoom (completed magnification), emitter (the camera), and eventType (eventType_ZoomComplete)\&. Return false to allow other handlers to run, or true to mark the event handled\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Handler with cancel() to remove this subscription\&.
.RE
.PP
Both \fBzoom()\fP and \fBzoomTo()\fP emit once per completed operation\&. Zero-duration operations emit synchronously unless queued or delayed; queued operations emit when advanced\&. Cancelled or replaced operations and \fBsetZoom()\fP do not emit\&. A shared camera emits once, independently of its number of attachments\&. Schedule pause delays completion\&. Restored scheduled operations emit on the restored camera; event handlers must be registered again after loading\&. Use camera\&.addHandler(handler, \fBpdg\&.eventType_ZoomComplete\fP) to listen with an \fBIEventHandler\fP directly\&. Completion belongs to \fBCamera\fP, replacing the former \fBSpriteLayer\fP action_ZoomComplete event and layer\&.onZoomComplete()\&. 
.PP
.nf
const subscription = camera\&.onZoomComplete(function(event) {
    console\&.log('Zoom completed at', event\&.zoom);
    return false;
});
camera\&.zoomTo(2, 0\&.5);
// Later: subscription\&.cancel();

.fi
.PP
 
