.SS "\fBCamera\fP whipPanTo (\fBCamera\fP destination, number seconds, int style = \fR\fBcamera_WhipLeft\fP\fP, number blur = \fR0\fP, int easing = \fR\fBeaseInOutQuad\fP\fP)"

.PP
Slide live camera outputs with optional directional motion blur\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fReasing:\fP \fBEasingFunction\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
The source slides out and the destination enters from the opposite edge\&. Offsets belong to composition: persistent camera location, following and parallax are unchanged\&. \fBCamera\fP opacity remains independent for each scene, and all samples clip to the common viewport\&. Blur averages eight nearby progress samples, with its spread fading to zero at the endpoints\&. The reference speed is one viewport per 0\&.65 seconds: halving the duration doubles blur spread, and doubling the duration halves it\&. Zero blur uses one sample\&. Both scenes continue rendering live; at completion the source hides and the destination shows\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdestination\fP Distinct camera attached to the same \fBPort\fP with the same nonempty viewport\&. 
.br
\fIseconds\fP Finite nonnegative duration in seconds\&. 
.br
\fIstyle\fP camera_WhipLeft (default), camera_WhipRight, camera_WhipUp or camera_WhipDown; names describe source travel\&. 
.br
\fIblur\fP Strength from 0 to 1, default 0\&. At the reference duration of 0\&.65 seconds, maximum sample spread is 15 percent of the viewport extent times this strength\&. Spread scales by 0\&.65 / seconds and is capped at one viewport extent for very fast pans\&. 
.br
\fIeasing\fP Easing function; defaults to easeInOutQuad\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This camera for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The source receives picking until completion\&. Shared transition ordering, pause, cancellation and snapshot restrictions apply\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
source\&.whipPanTo(destination, 0\&.4, pdg\&.camera_WhipLeft, 0\&.7);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBtransitionTo()\fP, \fBlumaFadeTo()\fP, \fBCamera visibility, fades and transitions\fP 
.RE
